<title>INDIA: Yield on Indian 364-day t-bill falls to 9.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Yield on Indian 364-day t-bill falls to 9.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Wednesday it raised the cut-off price to 91.76 rupees from 91.39 at its fortnightly auction of 364-day treasury bills.</p>
<p>Dealers said the yield dropped to 9.0 percent from 9.45.  </p>
<p>The RBI said it received 116 bids for 34.3 billion rupees of which it accepted 95 for 28.93 billion.</p>
<p>The weighted-average cut-off price worked out to 91.97 rupees, it said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
